[General] The variable is declared `thriftTelemetry` but `telemetry` is used on the next line — the snippet won't compile. Same in the two snippets below.

```suggestion
```java
// For server-side, decorate processor with a tracing wrapper.
TProcessor configureServer(OpenTelemetry openTelemetry, TProcessor processor, String serviceName) {
  ThriftTelemetry thriftTelemetry = ThriftTelemetry.create(openTelemetry);
  return thriftTelemetry.wrapServerProcessor(processor, serviceName);
```

[General] When `map.size > MAX_CONTEXT_ENTRIES`, this returns immediately without consuming the map entries from the protocol stream — `readMapEnd()` will be called in `finally` while the (potentially many) key/value bytes are still unread, leaving the protocol in a corrupt state for the rest of the message. The `MAX_CONTEXT_SIZE` branch below correctly skips remaining entries with `TProtocolUtil.skip(...)`; the same skipping is needed here.

```suggestion
      if (map.size > MAX_CONTEXT_ENTRIES) {
        logger.log(
            FINE,
            "Thrift context propagation entries count {0} exceeds maximum allowed of {1}, skipping context propagation.",
            new Object[] {map.size, MAX_CONTEXT_ENTRIES});
        for (int i = 0; i < map.size; i++) {
          TProtocolUtil.skip(protocol, TType.STRING);
          TProtocolUtil.skip(protocol, TType.STRING);
        }
        return emptyMap();
      }
```

