[General] If `currentScope.close()` throws, `instrumenter.end(...)` is never called and the span leaks. Consider closing the scope in a `try`/`finally` (or move the `instrumenter.end` call into a `finally` block).

```suggestion
  public void endSpan(@Nullable Throwable throwable, boolean failed) {
    if (currentScope == null || currentContext == null || currentRequest == null) {
      return;
    }
    try {
      currentScope.close();
    } finally {
      instrumenter.end(
          currentContext, currentRequest, failed ? ThriftResponseAccess.failed() : null, throwable);
    }
  }
```

